            <ArticleTitle>A novel ETFDH mutation in an adult patient with late-onset riboflavin-responsive multiple acyl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>291-294</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/00207454.2017.1380641</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM OF THE STUDY" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To report a novel mutation in the electron transfer flavoprotein dehydrogenase (ETFDH) gene in an adult patient with late-onset riboflavin-responsive multiple acyl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIALS AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">The genomic DNAs from a patient whose main clinical presentations are muscles weakness and hypoglycemia was analysed.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The patient was identified to carry compound heterozygous mutations in ETFDH gene. Two missense mutations c.814 G &gt; A and c.389 A &gt; T were found.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">This is the first report of c.814G &gt; A mutation in ETFDH in adult patient with MADD.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
